WEBVTT

00:25.741 --> 00:30.078
FOOL NIGHT

01:49.407 --> 01:50.659
Now, die!

02:15.976 --> 02:17.269
I'll get his head.

02:17.894 --> 02:19.771
I don't mind a double knockout.

02:22.899 --> 02:26.027
Oh, you came from Antarctica?

02:26.820 --> 02:30.115
And you call yourselves "Central," huh?

02:30.198 --> 02:31.700
Antarctica?

02:32.576 --> 02:36.329
That flower has memories
of coming here from Antarctica?

02:36.913 --> 02:37.747
I'll try touch--

02:47.632 --> 02:49.676
Excellent work, Mukuru.

02:50.385 --> 02:52.971
My lifespan has extended once again.

03:34.763 --> 03:39.100
Shiika is really nowhere to be found, huh?

03:39.893 --> 03:40.769
Yeah.

03:41.394 --> 03:44.022
These flowers are connected to life.

03:44.773 --> 03:49.027
The only things blooming here
are memories and emotions of the living.

03:49.861 --> 03:54.282
If she hadn't been made into a desk,
maybe I could've talked to her again.

03:56.952 --> 04:01.122
I left Shiika out in that back alley.

04:01.206 --> 04:04.501
I'd better hurry
and move her to a safe place.

04:06.628 --> 04:08.088
Then I guess it's farewell.

04:10.632 --> 04:13.718
Come on, mister. Be my friend.

04:17.514 --> 04:18.598
I can't.

04:19.975 --> 04:21.226
You can't forgive me?

04:22.018 --> 04:26.189
That wouldn't be fair
to all the people you murdered.

04:27.107 --> 04:30.360
You deserve to be punished.

04:31.903 --> 04:35.573
So, do you hate me?

04:45.125 --> 04:47.711
Okay, I'll get going.

04:51.715 --> 04:55.802
Right now, the doctor
and your girlfriend are fixing you up.

04:55.885 --> 04:57.095
She's not my girlfriend.

04:57.178 --> 05:00.515
I think you'll wake up
back in the real world soon.

05:05.687 --> 05:07.480
I hope we can meet again.

05:21.995 --> 05:22.954
Mukuru!

05:31.379 --> 05:34.591
My name is Toshiro Kamiya.

05:35.967 --> 05:38.845
That's all I wanted to say…

06:19.344 --> 06:20.178
You're awake!

06:22.639 --> 06:26.017
Seriously, thank goodness…

06:27.185 --> 06:28.853
Where's the doctor?

06:28.937 --> 06:32.273
Wait, the train stopped…

06:33.525 --> 06:35.693
Chill out. You just had a major operation.

06:37.654 --> 06:39.823
What the heck happened?

06:39.906 --> 06:42.242
<i>Dr. Kudai escaped.</i>

06:42.325 --> 06:46.162
<i>Ivy also disappeared</i>
<i>after taking down that space suit guy.</i>

06:46.246 --> 06:51.918
But this car is overflowing with records
of Ivy's seedling data and recovery.

06:52.544 --> 06:57.465
That's enough to prove that Dr. Kudai
and the opposition created Ivy.

06:57.549 --> 06:59.676
We got what we came for.

07:08.101 --> 07:10.979
I'm seriously starving…

07:13.314 --> 07:14.732
<i>Breaking news.</i>

07:14.816 --> 07:16.359
<i>It has been confirmed that</i>

07:16.443 --> 07:20.780
<i>Ken Hikasa from the Glory Days Party</i>
<i>aided research into murderous Spiriflora.</i>

07:21.364 --> 07:24.075
<i>His body was discovered</i>
<i>on an abandoned subway line.</i>

07:24.576 --> 07:26.244
<i>The police have seized documents</i>

07:26.327 --> 07:29.747
<i>describing research progress</i>
<i>and funding from the opposition…</i>

07:29.831 --> 07:30.915
You serious?!

07:30.999 --> 07:33.918
<i>…implying the existence</i>
<i>of a long-term scheme.</i>

07:34.002 --> 07:38.506
<i>The Glory Days Party has announced</i>
<i>that Hikasa acted independently</i>

07:38.590 --> 07:41.259
<i>and denied the party's involvement.</i>

07:41.342 --> 07:44.262
<i>The political world</i>
<i>is seeing widespread repercussions.</i>

08:22.592 --> 08:24.761
ABOLISH TRANSFLORATION!

08:29.641 --> 08:33.728
<i>The opposition's frequent protesting</i>
<i>has gradually calmed nationwide.</i>

08:34.562 --> 08:38.608
<i>Just now, the opposition announced</i>
<i>the disbandment of the Glory Days Party--</i>

08:55.208 --> 08:58.628
Dr. Kudai, why did you create Ivy?

08:58.711 --> 09:01.297
Why'd that armored space suit guy
attack us?

09:01.381 --> 09:05.260
Why is your name completely absent
from all documentation?

09:05.343 --> 09:07.220
What are you fighting against?

09:07.303 --> 09:12.767
Why must I answer such questions
from an enemy organization like yours?

09:13.810 --> 09:17.272
If we knew the truth,
maybe we wouldn't be enemies anymore.

09:17.355 --> 09:22.902
First of all, I don't want
the world knowing I'm alive.

09:23.486 --> 09:26.656
Well, actually,
whether I get rid of you or not,

09:26.739 --> 09:31.411
my work is scattered over these tracks,
so I suppose they'll find out eventually.

09:33.037 --> 09:34.289
Okay, I've decided.

09:35.039 --> 09:38.042
I command you to become my spy.

09:38.835 --> 09:43.131
If you agree, I'll answer your questions.

09:43.214 --> 09:47.719
Your mission is to identify
who's responsible for manufacturing him.

09:49.345 --> 09:51.556
<i>Toshiro was manufactured?</i>

09:51.639 --> 09:54.392
<i>Someone did this? It wasn't a coincidence?</i>

09:54.475 --> 09:55.518
<i>Why?</i>

09:55.602 --> 09:58.104
<i>And now Dr. Kudai wants me to be a spy?</i>

09:59.105 --> 10:00.440
<i>I couldn't…</i>

10:01.316 --> 10:02.942
<i>But what if I refuse?</i>

10:03.735 --> 10:07.447
<i>Ivy might come back</i>
<i>to attack me and Toshiro both…</i>

10:08.364 --> 10:12.827
By the way, I'm not interested
in doing anything to Transflora Medical.

10:12.910 --> 10:19.208
Of course, if they imploded from within,
I'd very much… very much enjoy that!

10:21.252 --> 10:26.215
However, my sole objective is to provide
a separate choice for humanity's future.

10:28.343 --> 10:32.680
Make a decision right now.
Will you spy for me? Or not?

10:33.931 --> 10:35.850
It's life or death.

10:46.819 --> 10:49.238
Very well. Ask me anything.

10:49.822 --> 10:51.449
First, why do I have to spy?

10:52.033 --> 10:56.829
I'm merely interested in joint research
with Toshiro's outstanding manufacturer.

10:56.913 --> 10:59.666
You just stated that
Transflora Medical is your enemy.

11:00.291 --> 11:04.837
Toshiro was seeded at Transflora Medical,
so wouldn't that researcher be your enemy?

11:05.546 --> 11:07.382
A clever one, you are.

11:07.465 --> 11:10.301
But I'm in no position to fuss over that.

11:12.512 --> 11:16.307
I don't have much time left, you see.

11:26.776 --> 11:30.363
I see you underwent transfloration.
But what are you--

11:30.446 --> 11:36.077
I'm trimming my decomposed organs
and flesh to delay the transfloration.

11:36.160 --> 11:40.706
I cannot clip the stem,
but the branches and leaves are fine.

11:41.207 --> 11:45.002
I've been surviving like this
for three years since my procedure.

11:45.086 --> 11:47.880
However, my limit is approaching.

11:48.464 --> 11:51.801
Moreover, the researcher
who manufactured Toshiro

11:51.884 --> 11:54.262
probably isn't my enemy.

11:55.763 --> 11:59.225
His research contradicts
Transflora Medical's principles.

11:59.308 --> 12:03.896
Perhaps they're a wandering genius
hiding research from Transflora Medical.

12:04.480 --> 12:08.443
Transflora Medical's principles?
Are you referring to oxygen generation?

12:08.526 --> 12:12.572
Yes, of course,
that's one of their major objectives,

12:12.655 --> 12:17.493
but first allow me to briefly explain
the origin of Transflora Medical.

12:18.202 --> 12:24.876
Around the year 2200, thick clouds
covered the planet and shut out the sun.

12:25.460 --> 12:31.007
Plants withered, and artificial satellites
became unable to transmit accurate data.

12:31.090 --> 12:33.634
Thus began one long, wintry night.

12:34.469 --> 12:37.346
<i>Earth was in danger of oxygen deficiency.</i>

12:37.430 --> 12:41.601
<i>Humanity's top biotechnology researchers</i>
<i>gathered from around the world</i>

12:41.684 --> 12:43.686
<i>to construct a research institute.</i>

12:43.769 --> 12:45.813
<i>It was named "Central."</i>

12:46.481 --> 12:48.608
<i>Their research bore fruit,</i>

12:48.691 --> 12:52.153
<i>recycling the human body</i>
<i>into an environmental conservation device.</i>

12:52.236 --> 12:55.531
<i>They successfully developed</i>
<i>transfloration technology.</i>

12:56.115 --> 13:01.078
However, Central refused
to undergo transfloration themselves.

13:01.162 --> 13:05.082
They pushed it onto everyone else
and secluded themselves in Antarctica.

13:05.166 --> 13:06.626
Cowardly, right?

13:06.709 --> 13:11.506
They're a group of bores
foolishly clinging to their human form.

13:12.089 --> 13:14.467
Central is lying in wait.

13:14.550 --> 13:19.222
They want all mainland humans
to undergo transfloration instead

13:19.305 --> 13:24.268
and produce a lush, green land
to enjoy hundreds of years from now.

13:25.478 --> 13:27.480
Transflora Medical
and the Transfloration Board

13:27.563 --> 13:31.025
are nothing more than
plant production factories

13:31.108 --> 13:34.737
constructed for the sake
of realizing Central's own principles.

13:36.322 --> 13:41.035
Admittedly, without them,
we would've died of oxygen deficiency.

13:41.118 --> 13:44.372
They don't deserve such one-sided hatred.

13:44.455 --> 13:45.665
That can't be…

13:46.499 --> 13:52.421
But they're trying to hinder the future
of transfloration for that very principle.

13:52.505 --> 13:55.758
They're forcing us to succumb
to our fate of becoming plants.

13:56.717 --> 13:59.262
I won't stand for it.

14:01.931 --> 14:07.144
Especially now that humanity's evolution
is within our grasp.

14:08.104 --> 14:12.942
Toshiro and Mukuru shall begin
an era of newly evolved humans.

14:13.025 --> 14:18.364
Finding Toshiro's manufacturer
will help us shape that future.

14:18.447 --> 14:20.366
Isn't that splendid?

14:20.449 --> 14:24.453
So, that armored space suit guy
was Central's agent sent to attack you?

14:24.537 --> 14:25.746
I'm sure he was.

14:26.247 --> 14:30.167
He came all this way
and failed to kill a senile old man…

14:30.251 --> 14:31.127
Doctor!

14:31.210 --> 14:32.587
It's time.

14:33.212 --> 14:36.257
Compile a report of your spy activities.

14:36.340 --> 14:39.802
I'll send a messenger to fetch it later…

14:43.389 --> 14:46.058
That reminds me, I never asked your name.

14:47.226 --> 14:49.061
I'm Yomiko Horai.

14:49.145 --> 14:52.607
"Yomi" refers to the underworld,
the place you ferry souls to.

14:52.690 --> 14:55.151
That name suits Transflora Medical well.

14:55.234 --> 14:56.527
Here's a souvenir.

15:01.866 --> 15:03.659
I won't be needing it.

15:31.228 --> 15:35.149
I take it you're the ones
responsible for this uproar?

15:36.734 --> 15:41.322
You successfully fought off the opposition
and cleared our name.

15:41.405 --> 15:42.615
You have my gratitude.

15:42.698 --> 15:43.950
Thank you.

15:44.033 --> 15:45.701
Uh, Director,

15:46.410 --> 15:49.664
what about the trials
and damages incurred after the uproar?

15:49.747 --> 15:53.042
Not to worry. We'll compensate for that.

15:53.709 --> 15:56.587
None of you individuals
will be held responsible.

15:57.630 --> 16:01.801
And, of course,
I'd like to reward each of you.

16:01.884 --> 16:05.137
If there's anything
I can do for you, ask away.

16:08.724 --> 16:09.684
Hire Toshiro Kamiya…

16:09.767 --> 16:11.018
Hire Saeko Kanaeno…

16:11.102 --> 16:14.063
…as an official employee
of Transflora Medical, please!

16:18.526 --> 16:19.944
And you, Hiragishi?

16:26.409 --> 16:27.994
I appreciate the offer,

16:28.077 --> 16:32.248
but would it be possible
to put my request on hold for now?

16:32.331 --> 16:34.917
You want me to owe you a favor?

16:35.835 --> 16:37.336
Is that a problem?

16:39.797 --> 16:41.507
As you wish.

16:42.717 --> 16:44.260
JOB OFFER LETTER

16:53.644 --> 16:57.523
Cheers to Takami, Asada, and Yorutake.

16:58.315 --> 17:00.985
This is for you guys.
Let's live it up tonight.

17:03.404 --> 17:05.614
That was one hell of a fight.

17:05.698 --> 17:09.618
White-hair acted like a dang fool, though.
Charging into that subway unarmed…

17:10.369 --> 17:12.747
Let me express my gratitude as well.

17:12.830 --> 17:15.416
Nice job protecting
Transflora Medical No. 4.

17:16.000 --> 17:19.545
Horai, Toshiro,
thanks for fighting for us.

17:20.337 --> 17:22.673
I can't believe you pulled it off…

17:23.382 --> 17:25.551
All righty then…

17:27.887 --> 17:29.055
Booze!

17:48.783 --> 17:51.202
<i>Yeah, I'm having a blast.</i>

17:52.995 --> 17:54.538
<i>This is great.</i>

17:55.206 --> 17:57.208
<i>I wish this party could go on forever.</i>

17:58.084 --> 18:00.002
<i>I wish time could just stop…</i>

18:01.796 --> 18:03.923
<i>I don't wanna be a Spiriflor…</i>

18:05.049 --> 18:06.926
<i>I wanna stay like this…</i>

18:08.511 --> 18:11.764
<i>Right here, with everyone…</i>

18:17.686 --> 18:18.854
I'm home.

18:58.435 --> 19:00.938
I'm at my breaking point.

19:26.922 --> 19:31.927
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

19:46.066 --> 19:47.359
Ms. Horai,

19:47.443 --> 19:50.738
there's a transfloration applicant
waiting at counter six.

19:50.821 --> 19:52.114
Okay.

20:09.006 --> 20:10.841
TRANSFLORATION REPORT
MEG OKUMURA

20:11.550 --> 20:14.970
From the Parade in Paupertown…

20:15.054 --> 20:16.055
It's coming.

20:17.973 --> 20:19.099
Morning…

20:22.019 --> 20:24.063
Morning will come…

20:27.024 --> 20:28.317
Morning…

20:40.955 --> 20:42.289
<i>Shine down on us…</i>

20:43.874 --> 20:44.875
<i>All of us…</i>

20:45.376 --> 20:48.545
<i>With love… and light…</i>

20:52.758 --> 20:55.511
Not her. Not this girl…

20:57.429 --> 20:58.931
I'll do something…

21:08.732 --> 21:14.613
PATIENT: KAORI KAMIYA
VISITOR: TOSHIRO KAMIYA

21:19.994 --> 21:23.789
Your mother is resting
in our heavy-lighting facility.

21:24.832 --> 21:27.251
She seems more anxious in the dark.

21:28.335 --> 21:29.628
Oh, okay.

21:56.780 --> 21:57.948
Hi, Mom.

21:59.408 --> 22:00.743
It's been a while.

22:12.004 --> 22:15.424
I'm not. I'm not at fault.

22:16.800 --> 22:20.679
I was tricked. That's why I just snapped.

22:22.097 --> 22:25.934
Someone is hiding the sunlight.

22:26.018 --> 22:28.187
I won't be fooled.

22:35.944 --> 22:36.945
Mom,

22:38.781 --> 22:43.577
I feel like I finally understand
what I'm supposed to do.

22:46.121 --> 22:48.040
I'm gonna help people.

22:52.586 --> 22:53.587
Uh-huh.

22:54.171 --> 22:57.466
Yeah. Yeah… Yeah.

23:01.804 --> 23:04.598
Got it. I'm on my way.

24:29.933 --> 24:34.938
Subtitle translation by: Logan Lampkins
